From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:31:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: asahi: enable CONFIG_EDAC for
 EDAC_APPLE_SOC

asahi.config requests CONFIG_EDAC_APPLE_SOC=m, but the menu it lives in
(CONFIG_EDAC) is not enabled by the fragment. With the official omarchy-pkgs
linux-aurora base config ("# CONFIG_EDAC is not set") the recipe's
validate-config step then fails on an unmet fragment line. Enable the menu
in the same fragment so the requested driver is actually built.

J604 note: measured on aurora-silicon integration/aurora 6ff31cbfa2
(7.3.0) with the official recipe config; configure_kernel failed before
this change.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
index 5581318240..0a5f6bc6cc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
@@ -155,6 +155,7 @@ CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS=y
 CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM=y
 CONFIG_UDMABUF=y
 CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
+CONFIG_EDAC=y
 CONFIG_EDAC_APPLE_SOC=m
 # Confine kernel executable code to a fixed physical CTXR window so the kernel
 # can run at EL2 on chips whose firmware locks the code-execute range. Inert
